  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "lesson_aotfw_001",
      "type": "lesson",
      "title": "Introduction to An Artist of the Floating World",
      "slug": "introduction_to_aotfw",
      "unit_id": "unit_aotfw",
      "sequence": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_l001_001",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "heading",
          "variant": "page",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": { "text": "Introduction to An Artist of the Floating World" },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l001_002",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "rich_text",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": {
            "html": "<p>Kazuo Ishiguro's <em>An Artist of the Floating World</em> (1986) is set in post-war Japan and narrated by Masuji Ono, a retired painter reflecting on a career entangled with nationalist propaganda. From the outset, the novel invites us to ask how personal memory shapes—and sometimes distorts—our sense of identity.</p>"
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l001_003",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "callout",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": {
            "style": "information",
            "title": "Key context",
            "body": "Japan's defeat in 1945 and the American occupation created social upheaval that reshaped how citizens understood loyalty, guilt, and cultural value."
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        }
      ],
      "status": "active",
      "created_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-02T09:00:00.000Z",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "tags": ["module-c", "introduction"],
      "syllabus_outcomes": ["EA12-8"],
      "outcome_ids": ["EA12-8"]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson_aotfw_002",
      "type": "lesson",
      "title": "Post-war Japan and Cultural Change",
      "slug": "postwar_japan_and_cultural_change",
      "unit_id": "unit_aotfw",
      "sequence": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_l002_001",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "heading",
          "variant": "page",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": { "text": "Post-war Japan and Cultural Change" },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l002_002",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "rich_text",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": {
            "html": "<p>Ono moves through a city rebuilding itself—new buildings beside bombed ruins, younger generations rejecting the values of their elders. Track how Ishiguro uses setting to mirror Ono's unstable recollection of his own past.</p>"
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l002_003",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "callout",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "teacher_only",
          "content": {
            "style": "teacher",
            "title": "Discussion prompt",
            "body": "Ask students to compare Ono's pride in his daughters' marriages with his evasiveness about his wartime posters. What does this tension suggest about selective memory?"
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        }
      ],
      "status": "active",
      "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-05T09:00:00.000Z",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "tags": ["module-c", "context"]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson_aotfw_003",
      "type": "lesson",
      "title": "Narrative Structure and Unreliable Memory",
      "slug": "narrative_structure_and_unreliable_memory",
      "unit_id": "unit_aotfw",
      "sequence": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_l003_001",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "heading",
          "variant": "section",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": { "text": "Unreliable narration" },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l003_002",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "rich_text",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "teacher_only",
          "content": {
            "html": "<p>Teacher note: Ono's first-person narration is deliberately inconsistent. Flag passages where he revises earlier claims—students should annotate these as evidence of self-justification rather than factual correction.</p>"
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "block_l003_003",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "callout",
          "variant": "medium",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": {
            "style": "remember",
            "title": "Analytical focus",
            "body": "When Ono recalls the 'floating world' of pleasure districts, consider whether nostalgia sanitises a culture he helped commodify for nationalist ends."
          },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
          "schema_version": 1
        }
      ],
      "status": "active",
      "created_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-08T09:00:00.000Z",
      "schema_version": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson_aotfw_004",
      "type": "lesson",
      "title": "Masuji Ono: Artist and Patriarch",
      "slug": "masuji_ono_artist_and_patriarch",
      "unit_id": "unit_aotfw",
      "sequence": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_l004_001",
          "type": "block",
          "block_type": "heading",
          "variant": "page",
          "visibility": "student_teacher",
          "content": { "text": "Masuji Ono: Artist and Patriarch" },
          "layout": {},
          "print": {},
          "settings": {},
          "created_at": "2026-01-10T09:00:00.000Z",
